-- statement:
--   Units $G=c=1$, signature $(-,+,+,+)$, $r_s=2M$, coordinates indexed $0,1,2,3$. **Standard** $(t,r,\theta,\varphi)$: $g^{\rm std}_M=\mathrm{diag}\big(-(1-\tfrac{2M}r),\ \tfrac1{1-2M/r},\ r^2,\ r^2\sin^2\theta\big)$, candidate inverse $\mathrm{diag}\big(-\tfrac1{1-2M/r},\ 1-\tfrac{2M}r,\ \tfrac1{r^2},\ \tfrac1{r^2\sin^2\theta}\big)$, domain $U^{\rm std}_M=\{r>0,\ r\neq2M,\ 0<\theta<\pi\}$. **Eddington–Finkelstein family** $(w,r,\theta,\varphi)$, $\varepsilon=1$ ingoing ($w=v$), $\varepsilon=-1$ outgoing ($w=u$): $g_{ww}=-(1-\tfrac{2M}r)$, $g_{wr}=g_{rw}=\varepsilon$, $g_{\theta\theta}=r^2$, $g_{\varphi\varphi}=r^2\sin^2\theta$, other entries $0$ (from $ds^2=-(1-r_s/r)dv^2+2\,dv\,dr+r^2d\Omega^2$, matrix entry $g_{vr}=1$, not $2$); candidate inverse $\hat g^{wr}=\hat g^{rw}=\varepsilon$, $\hat g^{rr}=1-\tfrac{2M}r$, $\hat g^{\theta\theta}=\tfrac1{r^2}$, $\hat g^{\varphi\varphi}=\tfrac1{r^2\sin^2\theta}$ (valid when $\varepsilon^2=1$); domain $U^{\rm EF}=\{r>0,\ 0<\theta<\pi\}$, which contains $r=2M$ when $M>0$. **Coordinate maps**: $\Phi_{M,\varepsilon}(t,r,\theta,\varphi)=(t+\varepsilon(r+2M\log\lvert r-2M\rvert),r,\theta,\varphi)$ (`toEF`) and $\Psi_{M,\varepsilon}(w,r,\theta,\varphi)=(w-\varepsilon(r+2M\log\lvert r-2M\rvert),r,\theta,\varphi)$ (`fromEF`); Mathlib's $\log$ is $\log|\cdot|$, so these are the usual $r+2M\ln|r-2M|$ on both sides of $r=2M$.
